  "metadata": {
    "type": "targeted_grid",
    "name": "knots_esp_line",
    "description": "Knots ESP Line: does the economic threshold hold under a real soft fork?\n\nPURPOSE: Re-test the prior economic_split findings with the real-fork\nmethod. The prior results were all produced by the legacy scripted\npartition (partition_miner_with_pools.py), where economic nodes never\nactually switch (F10's \"permanent lock\"):\n  - F7:  ESP at econ ~0.74 (v26_dominant at 0.70, v27_dominant at 0.78)\n  - F12: economic_split is the global separator at 2016-block;\n         PRIM v27 box economic_split >= 0.665\n  - F13: full-network transition-zone threshold ~0.563\nUnder --method inplace, economic/user nodes and pools really change what\ntheir node enforces (25 economic/user nodes switched within 15 minutes in\nthe 2026-09-27 smoke test), so this is where the threshold is most likely\nto move if the legacy method was biased.\n\nDESIGN:\n- 5 economic_split values x 2 seeds = 10 scenarios, plus the pilot's\n  E=0.55 as a sixth level\n- Each scenario run once per method from the same build manifest:\n    legacy   (prior method; the reference)\n    inplace  (real fork + real switching)\n    realfork (add only if the knots_method_pilot shows realfork and\n              inplace differ at E=0.55)\n  -> 20 runs (30 with realfork)\n- Network: full (realistic-economy-v2, 60 nodes)\n- Everything except economic_split fixed at the knots_method_pilot values,\n  so the pilot's violation_rate=1.00 scenarios are the E=0.55 point of\n  this line (same C, ideology, max_loss, seeds).\n- violation_rate 1.00 (legacy p=0.0): strict, the prior baseline.\n- Run settings: configs/knots_method_pilot_run.yaml (13000s, 10s\n  interval, 2016-block retarget).\n\nE VALUES: economic_split is quantized by whole economic nodes on the full\nnetwork. v27 custody share by E (2_build_configs, realistic-economy-v2):\n  E <= 0.42 -> 30.1%    0.44-0.56 -> 50.1%    0.58-0.66 -> 62.2%\n  0.68-0.72 -> 70.2%    0.74-0.78 -> 76.2%    0.80-0.82 -> 80.8%\nso one E per level (two E values in one level build identical networks):\n- 0.35 (30.1%): low anchor; tests whether real switching moves the\n        threshold down (expect v26 under legacy)\n- 0.55 (50.1%): the knots_method_pilot's violation_rate=1.00 runs\n- 0.62 (62.2%): F12's PRIM boundary level (0.665 is in this band)\n- 0.70 (70.2%): F7's v26 side\n- 0.78 (76.2%): F7's v27 side (the ESP flip is between 0.70 and 0.78)\n- 0.82 (80.8%): F8's economic override (expect v27 under every method)\n\nWHAT TO COMPARE (per E, legacy vs real-fork):\n- winner (legacy fork_convergence / real-fork outcomes.winner) -> where\n  the flip happens along E for each method\n- time of the first pool switch and of economic node switches\n- final economic weight per camp (legacy never moves; inplace can)\n- price gap trajectory\n\nDEPENDS ON: knots_method_pilot results (finishing ~2026-09-28 06:00). If\nthe pilot's methods agree at E=0.55, run legacy + inplace; if realfork\nand inplace differ, add realfork.\n",
